WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.535
-Oh, look at that!
Oh, look at that!

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.603
That's what I'm talking --
That is a friend right there.

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.672
-Look what I stole
from your show.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.708
-That is a friend.
No, that is a gift.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.142
Do you see --
You probably didn't even see,

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:11.510
but when you take a sip,

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:14.213
there's another bonus logo
on the bottom.

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:16.048
It's upside down, but whatever.

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:17.217
We'll fix it later.

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.784
It's for people with left --

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:21.053
Hey, yeah, that's what
I'm talking about!

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:23.489
"All About Steve."
-That was a lot of bourbon.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:26.526
I drank like half
a thing of bourbon.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.994
-Joel, what is
"All About Steve"?

00:00:28.994 --> 00:00:30.797
Is that that --

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.766
-My favorite movie of all time?
-Yeah.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:38.337
-This is Sandra Bullock,
who is, like, super famous.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.373
Bradley Cooper, super famous.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.743
Then we got Thomas Hayden
Church, Oscar nominee,

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.177
and then this guy --
I don't know who he is.

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:47.413
I think it's Ken Jeong.
He was in this thing.

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:48.881
I have no idea.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:52.719
I do a podcast with Ken, and
that movie had all the razzies,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.887
so I just make fun of him
endlessly.

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:56.723
-Why not?
That's what friends are for.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.124
See, Ken?
-Look at him.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:01.093
-That's what friends are for.
Come on.

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:03.329
-Yeah. And they're really
mocking his height

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.433
in this -- in this poster.
-[ Laughs ] Gosh.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:12.171
-Welcome to my -- Yeah, you like
how I chose an abandoned office

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:13.940
for the interview?

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.108
-I like that you dressed up.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.609
You look sharp.
You look great as always.

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.278
And I always appreciate you
coming on.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.678
You're glitching a bit now,

00:01:19.678 --> 00:01:21.714
which is good because it makes
me look better.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.249
You look like Max Headroom.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.886
-No. You look like Where's Waldo
on vacation.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.054
I like it.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:29.054 --> 00:01:30.790
-Or like you're
a gondola driver.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.424
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:35.562
Do they wear blazers?

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:38.064
-The gondola --
Oh, the gondola drivers?

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.499
-Yeah.
-No.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:42.401
You look like you're a gondola
driver going to First Communion.

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:49.609
Like, you're like, "Giuseppe, I
must become a --"

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.178
Sorry. You know what you're
dressed like, I think, Jimmy?

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.647
You're dressed like
a cool mega preacher.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.684
-Mm. Like "Ozark," one of those
dudes, like, on the boat?

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:00.452
That guy? Or like a Joel Osteen?

00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:03.690
-Like Joel Osteen. Yeah, now
they're all, like, hip.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.459
Like Justin Bieber's pastor.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.993
They, like, wear cool stuff

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:09.695
and they're always working out
and posting it.

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.531
That's what you look like.
That's a compliment.

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:14.868
-[ Laughs ]
God, I wish I was working out.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.802
I got to start working out.

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:18.937
What's your workout routine?
What do you do?

00:02:18.937 --> 00:02:21.674
What's in your --
What's in your workout routine?

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.177
-My wife and I usually --
We work out together,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:27.180
so we usually, like, uncork like
a white, like a Pinot Grigio.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.351
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:36.322
-And then we go right to
the red and then the hard stuff.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.824
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:41.327
I got to say I've been listening
to the podcast

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.597
that you've done with your pal
Ken Jeong, who we do love.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.100
That was cool,
but I didn't even know --

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.234
I knew you guys worked together.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.436
I didn't know you were
actual friends.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:53.138
-Thank you for mentioning that
we worked together.

00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:56.909
We were on a little show on NBC
called "Parks and Rec."

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:59.512
-Oh, close. "Community."

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.347
Same week.
You were on the same week.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:04.216
-I just want to say working with
Chris Pratt and Amy Poehler

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:07.687
was just some of the most fun
I've ever had on a show.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.922
-Yeah. Well, maybe one day
you'll work with them.

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.424
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.626
Ken and I started the podcast
because he --

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:14.827
It's called
"The Darkest Timeline,"

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:18.297
which is a thing
from "Community."

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:20.032
And Ken is a real doctor.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:23.102
He was a terrible doctor, and he
was thrown out of medicine.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.538
He was sued, and I want everyone
to know that.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:28.207
-That is not true.
Is that really true?

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:30.075
-Maybe.

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:34.713
So he knows what he's talking
about, and I'm an idiot.

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:37.516
-Ah.
-So it was me just kind of

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:40.953
talking to him about what was
happening with COVID

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:44.457
at the time, and then we began
inviting friends on.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.059
And so we've had --
It's been great.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.761
We've had, like,
the "Community" cast on,

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.529
and then Ken knows
a bunch of people.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:52.732
-Well, it's a funny show.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:56.569
I would encourage anyone
to go on it.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:59.972
Have you learned anything?
-Wait. You have a podcast yet?

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:01.174
-No.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:04.109
-You should make
time for podcasts

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:06.545
because it -- you would --

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:08.547
-I think so.
That's where we're going.

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:10.049
That's where we're headed?

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.885
-Yeah.
I mean, I think you'd be great.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:16.021
-Is the goal of a podcast
to just be the podcast

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:18.524
or would you want to end up
hosting the show

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.692
or like a TV show?

00:04:20.692 --> 00:04:23.963
-I would like to create
kind of a Ponzi scheme

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.698
where I take people's money
and eventually tell them

00:04:26.698 --> 00:04:29.568
they're going to make more
money, and then I run away

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:31.604
to a country where
they can't find me.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.406
-I've gotten e-mails from --
yeah, yeah, I can forward you

00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:35.975
some interesting places.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:39.078
-I'm sorry I haven't really
answered any of your questions

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:41.180
in a real way.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.349
-That's why we have you on.
You're a comedian. You're funny.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.151
You've been a great guest
on our show.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:48.487
I'm not necessarily sure
if we want the answer.

00:04:48.487 --> 00:04:51.024
-True. Do you want to see
my biggest joke so far?

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:52.125
-Yeah.

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.193
-Okay. Look.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.861
Hilarious.

00:04:55.861 --> 00:05:00.233
It's shorts with a suit!
[ Laughs ]

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:02.134
I'm sorry. That was really dumb.

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:04.370
-It actually really
made me laugh. I loved it.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.838
I thought it was
very, very funny.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.674
I appreciate you wearing the tie
and dressing up. It looks good.

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:11.210
-That's because I've become
a Mormon missionary,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:15.214
and so I've been going around.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.883
Everyone's home. It's great.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.317
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:20.420
I guess so.
It's good for business, sure.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.188
There's more to talk about.

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:24.256
I do want to
talk about "Community."

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:25.758
There's lots of things
I want to talk to you about,

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:27.693
and, of course, "Card Sharks."

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:30.730
-And I want to know what you did
for the last two weeks.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.532
-I got tan.

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:35.268
-You look good.
Did you go to Long Island?

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:37.070
-[ Laughs ]

